    <string name="help_adb_mirroring_body">Only available in LAN/USB mode. Install android-platform-tools and scrcpy on Mac, enable Wireless Debugging in Android Developer Options, and pair via ADB QR code in AirSync on Mac.</string>
    <string name="help_getting_started_body">For local LAN mode, keep your Android and Mac on the same Wi-Fi network, then scan the QR code shown in AirSync on Mac or enter IP/port/key manually.</string>
    <string name="help_permissions_body">• Notification Access: Required for notification &amp; media sync (enable Restricted Settings in App Info for sideloaded APKs).\n• Post Notifications: Shows ongoing connection status.\n• Ignore Battery Optimization: Keeps background sync alive.\n• Storage (Optional): For wallpaper sync and local file access.</string>
    <string name="help_reconnection_body">When disconnected unexpectedly, AirSync automatically retries in the background. You can also tap the Quick Settings tile to reconnect or pause anytime.</string>
    <string name="help_relay_body">Relay mode lets you sync notifications, text clipboard, battery status, and media controls across different networks via your own WSS relay server. Enter identical server URL, room, room secret (≥16 chars), and copy the AES key from Mac. Leave cert fingerprint blank for CA-signed HTTPS domains, or enter the 64-char SHA-256 hex fingerprint for self-signed certs.</string>
    <string name="help_troubleshooting_body">• Notification stopped syncing: Re-open the app or check Notification Access permission.\n• Relay auth failed: Confirm the AES key from Mac matches and room secret is ≥16 chars.\n• LAN IP not found: Check Wi-Fi AP isolation or VPN routing.</string>
