    <string name="permission_background_why">Android aggressively stops background apps to save battery. Exempting AirSync from battery optimization keeps your connection and notification sync reliable when the app is in the background.</string>
    <string name="permission_clipboard_a11y_button">Agree and open settings</string>
    <string name="permission_clipboard_a11y_desc">Recommended: sync copied text to your Mac automatically</string>
    <string name="permission_clipboard_a11y_explain">Android does not let apps read the clipboard in the background. With this optional Accessibility service enabled, AirSync can detect when you copy text in any app and send it to your Mac automatically. Without it, you can still send your clipboard using the share sheet, the Quick Settings tile or shortcuts.</string>
    <string name="permission_clipboard_a11y_title">Background Clipboard Sync</string>
    <string name="permission_clipboard_a11y_why">AirSync uses the Accessibility API only to detect copy actions (such as tapping "Copy" or a "Copied to clipboard" message). When a copy is detected, AirSync briefly opens an invisible window to read the clipboard and sends the text to your paired Mac.\n\nWhat AirSync does NOT do with this permission:\n• It does not read or store screen content, messages or passwords\n• It does not record keystrokes or perform actions on your behalf\n• It does not share any data with third parties or upload it to any server\n\nClipboard text is only sent to your own paired Mac over your encrypted local connection, and only while connected. You can turn this off at any time in Android Accessibility settings.\n\nBy tapping "Agree and open settings" you consent to this use.</string>
    <string name="permission_local_network_button">Grant Local Network Access</string>
    <string name="permission_local_network_explain">AirSync needs access to your local network to discover and connect to your Mac over Wi-Fi.</string>
    <string name="permission_local_network_title">Local Network Access</string>
    <string name="permission_local_network_why">Local network discovery allows the app to find and establish a secure, fast connection with your Mac on the same Wi-Fi network for syncing notifications, clipboard, and controlling media controls. Without this, Wi-Fi synchronization cannot function on Android 17+.</string>
    <string name="permission_notif_access_why">This is the core permission for AirSync. Without it, AirSync cannot forward notifications or media playback status to your Mac. Data is always sent over your encrypted connection.</string>
    <string name="permission_post_notif_why">AirSync uses notifications to show connection status, file transfer progress, and link actions.</string>
    <string name="permission_storage_why">This optional permission is only used in local LAN mode for wallpaper sync and mounting/browsing phone storage from your paired Mac.</string>
